<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Reaction Stickers</p>

      <h1>Reaction Sticker Maker</h1>

      <p>
        Make expressive reaction stickers for chats, communities, comments, and social posts. Create
        happy, sad, surprised, angry, cozy, and playful sticker ideas from prompts or portraits.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#generator">Make Reaction Stickers</a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Emotion-first prompts</h2>

        <p>
          Start with one reaction, then add the character, object, mood, and sticker style so the
          result reads quickly in chat.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Small sticker sets</h2>

        <p>
          Add one prompt per line to generate a small batch of related reactions with a consistent
          subject and style.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Downloadable files</h2>

        <p>
          Review results in history, retry failed prompts, favorite strong reactions, and download
          PNG or WebP files.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to make a reaction sticker</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>
          Choose one emotion or message, such as excited, sleepy, shocked, proud, or confused.
        </li>
        <li>Pick a subject, such as a mascot, pet, avatar, snack, object, or portrait.</li>
        <li>
          Add sticker-style words like clean border, simple background, and readable expression.
        </li>
        <li>Generate, compare results in history, and download PNG or WebP files.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Reaction sticker prompt examples</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>
          happy panda reaction sticker, big smile, clean white border, simple background
        </code>
        <code>surprised cat sticker, wide eyes, bold outline, rounded chat icon style</code>
        <code>sleepy coffee cup reaction sticker, cozy mood, soft colors, crisp silhouette</code>
        <code>
          angry tiny robot sticker, funny expression, bright accent, clean sticker frame
        </code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Build a reaction sticker set</h2>

      <p>
        A good reaction sticker set keeps one subject and changes the emotion. Try the same mascot
        as happy, shocked, sleepy, confused, proud, and cheering. This makes the set feel consistent
        while covering more chat situations.
      </p>

      <p>
        The app creates downloadable sticker files. Uploading, packaging, or size-checking for a
        specific chat platform happens outside the app.
      </p>

      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/custom-sticker-maker"}>Custom Sticker Maker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/sticker-maker-online"}>Sticker Maker Online</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/cute-sticker-ideas"}>Cute Sticker Ideas</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>What is a reaction sticker?</summary>

        <p>
          A reaction sticker is a small expressive image used to respond in chats, comments,
          communities, or social posts.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I make a reaction sticker set?</summary>

        <p>
          Yes. Add one emotion prompt per line to make a small set with a consistent subject and
          sticker style.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does this upload stickers to chat apps?</summary>

        <p>
          No. AI Sticker Maker generates downloadable sticker files. Platform upload, sticker pack
          setup, and size checks happen outside the app.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
